{
  "_what": "Authoring input for gates/golden_publish.py. These are complete canonical records, published over the write surface and then compared field by field against this file. Both publishable 1.8 types require every member, so a record is whole or it is rejected; there is no patch form to author.",
  "_rules": [
    "Expected values come from this file, never from the gateway. A gate that asked the endpoint what it stored and then checked it served that would pass for any endpoint, including a broken one.",
    "Identity fields (provider_id, org) are in the body here because this batch reads them from the request. 1.9 candidate entry 4 records that they should come from the credential instead; when they do, this file loses them and the gate checks the server set them.",
    "The authority in every URI is demo.spatialdds.org, so these records are only acceptable to an endpoint serving as that authority.",
    "TopicMeta entries carry durability since the 1.8 revision (spec 9c3e1f2, closing finding 17). The value is TRANSIENT_LOCAL because the topics this announce describes are latched definitions. Before the revision the member did not exist and a bridged gateway had nowhere to read N.7's required manifest durability from; now it does, and the gateway's own manifest and this record are checked against each other per topic by gates/anchor_serve.py."
  ],
