    "changed": {
      "envelope": "Wrapped in the {id, profile, rtype, service} envelope \u00a73.3.0's own prose example uses. The source file has none, so nothing in it states the URI it answers to and \u00a77.5.2 cannot resolve it -- finding 28.",
      "schema_version": "Dropped. The source says `spatial.core/1.7` inside the v1.8 directory, and \u00a72 establishes `profile: spatial.manifest/1.8` as the manifest profile string. Wrong key, stale value -- finding 27.",
      "auth": "oauth2/auth.acme.com -> bearer against this authority, which is what this endpoint actually accepts.",
      "coverage": "SF bbox -> a declared circle at the fountain, the form \u00a73.3.4 prefers for a footprint someone chose, matching the recording's own announce.",
      "transforms": "Omitted. The source's example transforms a ship-fixed frame to earth-fixed; a fixed VPS at a fountain has nothing to transform, and inventing one would be worse than its absence.",
      "$comment keys": "Dropped. They are documentation in the source, not record data.",
      "ttl_sec": "Added, 1800. \u00a77.5.2 lets a manifest govern its own cache lifetime and the N.4 erratum makes that the max-age; a manifest without one takes the resolver default."
    }
